Reasons for Postponement
While fans have been eagerly awaiting Radiohead's European tour, it was announced last week that the band has decided to postpone their shows. The decision comes amidst the ongoing global COVID-19 pandemic, which has forced many artists to cancel or reschedule live events. 

The primary reason for the postponement is the safety and well-being of the band, their crew, and most importantly, their fans. With the pandemic still ongoing and travel restrictions being enforced in many countries, it has become increasingly difficult for large-scale events to be organized safely. Moreover, the uncertainty surrounding the pandemic makes it difficult for the band to guarantee that the shows could proceed without compromising on precautions and guidelines.

