extension = ".pdf"
files = get_files_with_extension(directory, extension)
print(files)
```

This code uses the `os.walk()` function to iterate over all the files in the directory and its subdirectories. It checks if each file ends with the specified extension using the `endswith()` method. If it does, it adds the full path of the file to the `files` list. Finally, it returns the list of files with the specified extension.
