3. The algorithm should handle different compounding intervals, such as daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, or annually, specified by the user.
4. The algorithm should take into account any additional fees or charges associated with the interest calculation, specified by the user.
5. The algorithm should handle different types of interest rates, such as fixed, variable, or floating rates, specified by the user.
